Certainly! Here's a simple JavaScript function that switches the order of adjectives in a sentence:

```javascript
function switchAdjectives(sentence) {
  // Split the sentence into an array of words
  const words = sentence.split(" ");

  // Filter out the adjectives
  const adjectives = words.filter(word => word.match(/^[a-z]+$/));

  // Reverse the order of the adjectives
  const reversedAdjectives = adjectives.reverse();

  // Join the reversed adjectives back into a sentence
  const newSentence = reversedAdjectives.join(" ");

  return newSentence;
}

// Test the function with your example sentence
const inputSentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const outputSentence = switchAdjectives(inputSentence);
console.log(outputSentence); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```

This function first splits the sentence into an array of words using the `split()` method. It then filters out the adjectives using a regular expression that matches any word containing only letters (`/^[a-z]+$/`). Finally, it reverses the order of the adjectives using the `reverse()` method and joins them back into a sentence using the `join()` method. The resulting sentence is returned by the function.

