To retrieve the username from the JWT token in ASP.NET Core Web API, you can use the `JwtSecurityTokenHandler` class to decode the token and extract the username claim. Here's an example of how to do this:

1. First, make sure you have installed the `Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens` package using NuGet.

2. In your WebApi project, create a new class that will handle the token decoding and claim extraction. For example:

```csharp
using Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens;
using System;
using System.Security.Claims;
using System.Text;

public class JwtTokenHandler
{
    public static string ExtractUsernameFromToken(string token)
    {
        var tokenHandler = new JwtSecurityTokenHandler();
        var key = Encoding.ASCII.Parse("your_secret_key");
        var tokenValidationParameters = new TokenValidationParameters
        {
            IssuerSigningKey = key,
            ValidateIssuer = false,
            ValidateAudience = false,
            ValidateLifetime = true,
            ClockSkew = TimeSpan.Zero
        };

        var securityToken = tokenHandler.ReadJwtToken(token, tokenValidationParameters);
        var usernameClaim = securityToken.Claims.FirstOrDefault(c => c.Type == "username");
        return usernameClaim?.Value;
    }
}
```

