To create a simple toast notification using React Context, follow these steps:

1. Create a `ToastContext` file:

```javascript
import React, { createContext, useState } from 'react';

const ToastContext = createContext();

function ToastProvider(props) {
  const [toastMessages, setToastMessages] = useState([]);

  function addToastMessage(message) {
    setToastMessages((prevMessages) => [...prevMessages, message]);
  }

  return (
    <ToastContext.Provider value={{ toastMessages, addToastMessage }}>
      {props.children}
    </ToastContext.Provider>
  );
}

export { ToastContext, ToastProvider };
```

2. Create a `Toast` component:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { useContext } from 'react';
import { ToastContext } from './ToastContext';

function Toast() {
  const { toastMessages } = useContext(ToastContext);

  return (
    <div className="toast-container">
      {toastMessages.map((message) => (
        <div key={message} className="toast">{message}</div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}

export default Toast;
```

3. Use the `ToastProvider` and `Toast` components in your application:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { ToastProvider, Toast } from './ToastContext';

function App() {
  return (
    <ToastProvider>
      <Toast />
      {/* Add your application content here */}
    </ToastProvider>
  );
}

export default App;
```

Now you have a simple toast notification system using React Context. You can use the `addToastMessage` function to add new toast messages to the list. The `Toast` component will display the list of toast messages.

